<!DOCTYPE suzuki [
<!ENTITY % sdatacharaents SYSTEM "..\config8\sdatacharaents.txt">
%sdatacharaents;
]>
<suzuki><manual>
<section sectnbr = "5A">
<servcat sctnbr = "05" scnbr = "01">
<configtype typenbr = "0">
<servinfotype sitcode = "6">
<servinfo servinfosgmlid = "AENLSB0A5106039" svcinfotypenbr = "08" svcinfoqualnbr = "03" page = "2" supplyoff = "1" modify = "0">
<title>
Input Shaft Speed Sensor Inspection
</title>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A5106038">Input Shaft Speed Sensor Removal and Installation</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove input shaft speed sensor. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A5106038"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check the following point.
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
End face of input shaft speed sensor and direct clutch drum teeth are free from any metal particles and damage.
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check input shaft speed sensor as follows.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If faulty condition is found, replace input shaft speed sensor. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A5106038"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Connect battery (1), resistance and ammeter (3) to input shaft speed sensor connector (4) as shown in figure.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IEL10C510283.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "55.294mm" ver = "02" gw = "200" gh = "140"/>
<callout>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<tgroup cols = "2" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<colspec colnum = "1" colname = "1" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "2" colname = "2" colwidth = "1.378in"/>
<tbody>
<row rowsep = "0">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
2.
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Resistance (100 &#937;)
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</callout>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>
Check that current through input shaft speed sensor changes to specified value when ferromagnetic material (iron) (1) passes in front of input shaft speed sensor (2).
</ptxt>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
The gap “a” between ferromagnetic material (iron) and end face of input shaft speed sensor must be 5 mm (0.2 in.) or less.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
<spec>
<title>
Input shaft speed sensor current
</title>
<ptxt>
Current alternates between 4 – 8 mA and 12 – 16 mA
</ptxt>
</spec>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IEL10C510287.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "56.058mm" ver = "01" gw = "185" gh = "142"/>
</figure>
</s2>
</s1>
</servinfo>
</servinfotype>
</configtype>
</servcat>
</section></manual></suzuki>
